-- title:
--   Height 4 of the formal group of a fake elliptic curve
-- statement:
--   Fix rationals $a,b$, a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule $\Lambda$ of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, a natural number $N$ and a prime $q$. Let $\mathrm{coord}:\Lambda\to W(\mathbb{F}_{q^2})\times W(\mathbb{F}_{q^2})$ satisfy `IsOrderCoord`: it is additive, injective, sends $1$ to $(1,0)$, has dense image modulo every power of $q$, satisfies the twisted multiplication rule $\mathrm{coord}(mm')=(\alpha\alpha'+q\beta\,\sigma(\beta'),\ \alpha\beta'+\beta\,\sigma(\alpha'))$ for $\mathrm{coord}(m)=(\alpha,\beta)$, $\mathrm{coord}(m')=(\alpha',\beta')$ and $\sigma$ the Witt-vector Frobenius, and has $\alpha+\sigma(\alpha)$ equal to the reduced trace whenever $m+\bar m$ is an integer; assume $1\in\Lambda$. Let $B$ be an Artinian local commutative ring in which $q$ is nilpotent, and $B_0$ a commutative $B$-algebra such that $B\to B_0$ is surjective with nilpotent kernel ideal. Let $E_0$ be a fake elliptic curve over $B_0$ of level $N$ with $\Lambda$-action, let $X$ be a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module over $B$ for $q$ (a commutative two-dimensional formal group law $X.F$ with $W(\mathbb{F}_{q^2})$-action and uniformiser $\varpi$ satisfying $\varpi\circ\varpi=[q]$ and $\varpi\circ\mathrm{act}(\alpha)=\mathrm{act}(\sigma\alpha)\circ\varpi$), and let $\theta_0$ be a system of formal coordinates in two variables for $E_0.f$ exhibiting, via `IsFormalModuleVia`, the base change of $X$ to $B_0$ as the formal module of $E_0$ compatibly with $\mathrm{coord}$ and the $\Lambda$-action. Then for every field $k$ and every surjective ring homomorphism $\rho:B\to k$, the quotient of $k[[x_1,x_2]]$ by the ideal generated by the two components of the $q$-th iterated series $[q]$ of the formal group law $X.F$ pushed forward along $\rho$ has $k$-dimension $q^4$.
--
--   This is the statement that the two-dimensional formal group attached to a fake elliptic curve has height $4$ at a prime $q$ ramified in the quaternion order, expressed concretely as the $q$-torsion subscheme of the formal group being finite flat of rank $q^{2\cdot 2}$ over each residue field of the base. It is the numerical input to the deformation-theoretic lifting step for fake elliptic curves over Artinian local bases used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation.
